**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Each group of a split file is matched to an experiment by the naming template, and an unmatched group the template can read is offered the setup and the experiment its name describes (001 §K 'match each group by the naming template, list the unmatched groups and offer to create setups for them (the template parse supplies slots and angles)'; 001 §P `MatchByTemplate`; the S9.1 mapper's request: an experiment made from a group is named by `experimentNameAmong` with the read name's note, or the key). Nothing is written here: the window applies a split in step 320. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/DataSplits.fs` (step 317), after `splitGroups`, each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `type DataRowKey with member this.nameText : NameText`, a key as a name the template reads (step 269), as `MuellerExperimentLabel.nameText` is (step 270); no member converts back (ELEV006). (2) `DataSplitError`, an `*Error` union whose cases carry the error that stopped the group: `SplitKeyTextErr of ExperimentError` (the key is no experiment name, step 286), `SplitKeyNameErr of NamingTemplateError` (the template does not read the key, or the key names no item, steps 268-271), `SplitKeySetupErr of SetupError` (the table cannot hold the key's items and angles, steps 255, 274) and `SplitKeyTwiceErr of reason : string` (an earlier group matched the same experiment), with `member this.describe : string` rendering `the key is no experiment name: <e.describe>`, `the key does not read through the naming template: <e.describe>`, `the table cannot hold the key's setup: <e.describe>` and `two groups match one experiment: <reason>`. (3) `SplitSetupOffer = { setup : Setup; experiment : ExperimentName }`, a setup (held, or new) and the new experiment the group would be attached to; `SplitGroupMatch` = `ExperimentForGroup of experiment : ExperimentName` (the kit's experiment of that name) | `SetupOfferForGroup of offer : SplitSetupOffer` | `GroupWithoutMatch of problem : DataSplitError`; `SplitGroup = { key : DataRowKey; points : MeasuredPointCount; matching : SplitGroupMatch }`; and `DataSplit = { groups : SplitGroup list }`. A split is never stored, so no wire tag is added. (4) `[<ReferenceEquality>] DataSplitParam = { template : NamingTemplate; experiments : Experiment list; setups : Setup list; table : SetupSlot list; items : Item list; choiceOf : Item -> ItemModelChoice option }`, the kit's template, experiments, setups and items, the table, and how an item resolves to its model (the window's `tryItemModelChoice`, step 263). (5) `static member DataSplit.ofGroups (param : DataSplitParam) (groups : KeyedGroup list) : DataSplit`, the one matching rule, group by group in order. (a) The key's name: `key.nameText.toExperimentName` (step 286); an error is `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeyTextErr e)`. (b) An experiment of `param.experiments` whose `name.fileStem` equals that name's ignoring case (the kit's name identity, step 286) matches: `ExperimentForGroup` of its name, the first in list order. (c) Otherwise `param.template.readName key.nameText` (step 269), an error being `SplitKeyNameErr`; its `writeName` made an `ExperimentName` (the name the template would give, `-(QZ#45.0)-` read back as `-(QZ#45)-`) matches an experiment of that file stem the same way. (d) Otherwise the group is offered: the reading's items are `param.template.itemsOf reading param.items` (step 271), an error being `SplitKeyNameErr`. Over `SetupSlot.inLightOrder param.table` (step 257), every slot whose role a `SlotPlaceholder` of the template's `pieces` names takes a `SlotChoice` (step 274): the item the reading names in that role, or nothing when it names none, turned for an `ObjectSlotRole k` with a read angle to that angle for a `FixedMounting` item and to `sign.physicalAngleOf item.dialZeroAngle angle` for a `DialMounted sign` item (steps 255, 258), so the recorded reading is the name's, and otherwise keeping the slot's `placement.r1`; every other slot is left as the table holds it. A role the reading names and the table has no slot of is `SplitKeySetupErr (UnknownSetupSlotErr <the key and the role's text>)`. The setup is `generate` (step 274) of the grid of those one-choice axes over `param.table`, `param.items`, `param.choiceOf` and `param.template`, held being `param.setups` followed by the setups offered to earlier groups, so two groups whose keys describe one setup are offered the same one; its error is `SplitKeySetupErr`. The experiment is `param.template.experimentNameAmong setup.slots param.items reading.noteOpt taken <the key's name>` (step 286), `taken` being the names of `param.experiments` and of the experiments offered to earlier groups. (e) A group whose matched experiment an earlier group matched is `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeyTwiceErr <both keys and the name>)`. Members of `DataSplit`, each a filter of `groups` in order: `this.matched`, `this.offered` and `this.unmatched`. No cache, sort, fuzzy match or other member is added. Tests, in `DataSplitTests` (step 317), over test-local copies of step 271's slots (`src`, `lpA`, `sampleA`, `sampleB`, `lpB`, `det`), items (`Laser`, `CPL1`, `CPL2`, `QZ`, `LR`, `QZd` dial-mounted with its zero at 10°) and template `lab`, with a `choiceOf` answering each item's choice: `a group matches the experiment its key names, as written or as the template writes it back`: with the experiments `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL` and `E2`, `ofGroups` of the group `cpl-(qz#45-lr#45)-cpl` alone matches the first by its name, of `CPL-(QZ#45.0-LR#45)-CPL` alone matches it by its written name, and of `e2` matches `E2`. `an unmatched group the template reads is offered its setup and experiment over the table's slots`: with no experiment and no held setup, `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL-2` is offered a new setup whose `lpA` holds `CPL1`, `sampleA` `QZ` at R1 90°, `sampleB` nothing and `lpB` `CPL2`, named `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL`, and the experiment `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL-2`; a later group `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL-BR` is offered that same setup and `CPL-(QZ#90)-CPL-BR`; with that setup held, the offer is the held setup itself; `CPL-(QZd#-20)-CPL` places `QZd` at R1 30° recorded as the reading −20°. `an unmatched group the template cannot place is listed with its reason, and two groups never share an experiment`: `Darkness` and `CPL-(XX#0)-CPL` are `GroupWithoutMatch (SplitKeyNameErr _)`; over a table without `sampleB`, `CPL-(QZ#0-LR#0)-CPL` is `SplitKeySetupErr` naming `Obj 2`; the groups `CPL-(QZ#45-LR#45)-CPL` and `CPL-(QZ#45.0-LR#45)-CPL` with that experiment held match it once and refuse the second with `SplitKeyTwiceErr` naming both keys; `matched`, `offered` and `unmatched` list the groups in order. `every split error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local payload renders a distinct text holding it. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved.

**Acceptance.** After matching lands, `DataSplit.ofGroups` MUST match each group to the kit's experiment its key names, as written or as the template writes it back, offer an unmatched group the template can read the setup (held or new) and experiment its name describes over the table's slots and angles, and list every other group with its typed reason, two groups never matching one experiment; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a group matches the experiment its key names, as written or as the template writes it back`, `an unmatched group the template reads is offered its setup and experiment over the table's slots`, `an unmatched group the template cannot place is listed with its reason, and two groups never share an experiment` and `every split error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
